WEBVTT

00:00:00.059 --> 00:00:01.809
Welcome to Resgrid Academy.

00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:06.000
In this lesson, we will put the right resgrid app on each device.

00:00:06.409 --> 00:00:09.880
A configured department still needs members and shared devices to

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:13.060
sign in to the correct department with the correct permissions.

00:00:13.439 --> 00:00:16.579
We will explain the features, the setup decisions, and a

00:00:16.579 --> 00:00:18.479
practical way to check the result.

00:00:19.010 --> 00:00:24.069
Members install the Responder app, a tablet in Engine 1 runs the Unit app and

00:00:24.069 --> 00:00:26.029
a station screen shows the Big Board.

00:00:26.549 --> 00:00:29.150
Most members use Resgrid through the Responder app.

00:00:29.589 --> 00:00:33.610
Getting everyone installed and signed in is what lets dispatches reach them.

00:00:34.129 --> 00:00:37.540
The examples in this series use a fictional department and are teaching

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:39.780
scenarios, not default settings.

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:41.760
Responder application.

00:00:42.229 --> 00:00:46.439
The member app for receiving dispatches, responding and setting status.

00:00:46.889 --> 00:00:51.720
Have every member install the Responder app, sign in and allow notifications.

00:00:52.349 --> 00:00:53.420
Unit application.

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:56.770
The in-vehicle app that represents an apparatus.

00:00:57.159 --> 00:01:01.459
Install the Unit app on each apparatus tablet and select its unit.

00:01:02.079 --> 00:01:03.380
Dispatch application.

00:01:03.799 --> 00:01:06.770
The dispatcher view for creating and managing calls.

00:01:07.159 --> 00:01:11.380
Give dispatch access to the people who dispatch, then have them sign in.

00:01:12.199 --> 00:01:14.189
Incident command and accountability.

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:18.130
Incident command and accountability for incident commanders.

00:01:18.659 --> 00:01:21.949
Give command access to the officers who run incidents.

00:01:22.569 --> 00:01:23.229
Big Board.

00:01:23.689 --> 00:01:26.869
A station display of calls, units and personnel.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:30.829
Open the Big Board on a station screen and choose what it shows.

00:01:31.499 --> 00:01:32.130
Dashboard.

00:01:32.619 --> 00:01:36.759
The department home page: current status, staffing and activity.

00:01:37.169 --> 00:01:40.549
Decide which devices each role will use and share the app

00:01:40.549 --> 00:01:42.150
download links with your members.

00:01:42.749 --> 00:01:43.659
My Profile.

00:01:44.050 --> 00:01:48.009
Your own profile, contact details and notification preferences.

00:01:48.370 --> 00:01:51.740
Decide which devices each role will use and share the app

00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:53.299
download links with your members.

00:01:53.969 --> 00:01:54.949
Your Departments.

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:57.389
Switch between the departments you belong to.

00:01:57.929 --> 00:02:01.370
Decide which devices each role will use and share the app

00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:02.959
download links with your members.

00:02:03.599 --> 00:02:06.299
For the training scenario, work in this order.

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:07.309
Step 1.

00:02:07.869 --> 00:02:11.539
Set up a member device with Responder and notification permissions.

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:12.689
Step 2.

00:02:13.130 --> 00:02:16.510
Set up an apparatus tablet with Unit and select its unit.

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:17.640
Step 3.

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:22.630
Grant appropriate Dispatch or Command access and configure a station Big Board.

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:24.730
Now verify the result.

00:02:25.249 --> 00:02:28.469
Check the active department, device identity, and a

00:02:28.510 --> 00:02:30.110
controlled notification test.

00:02:30.590 --> 00:02:32.950
Check what a shared station screen exposes.

00:02:33.469 --> 00:02:38.230
A common problem to watch for: Installing an app does not prove alerts arrive.

00:02:38.730 --> 00:02:43.210
Verify OS notification and location settings on the actual device used.

00:02:43.939 --> 00:02:45.509
Your practice task is simple.

00:02:45.909 --> 00:02:50.390
Use a sample member, unit tablet, dispatcher, and station display to

00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:52.209
follow the same training incident.

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:54.909
Record which devices complete the test.

00:02:55.270 --> 00:02:59.220
Record the result, who owns the follow-up, and when it should be reviewed.

